# Simplification candidates — merged owner list

2026-11-08. Sources: final sections of [Codex](simplify_codex.out), [Kimi](simplify_kimi.out), and [agy](simplify_agy.out). “ASK” normalizes “WORTH ASKING.” “not raised” means no verdict on that specific candidate in that reviewer’s simplification answer; broader KEEP comments are not manufactured into votes on every subproposal. Overlapping bundles are split where their verdicts or effects differ.

All anchors below were checked against the repository. Decisions govern over legacy prose and implementation. CHANGE means **recommend an owner-approved revision**, not a decision or permission to implement. Exact unapproved replacement spellings are marked ILLUSTRATIVE. Reasons are at most 60 words each; workload benefits are judgments, not measured results. No language changes have been made.

Ordered first by cross-review agreement and owner importance, then actionable surface reductions, unresolved semantic changes, and confirmed KEEP distinctions. The three reviewers have not reviewed this merged artifact.

## 1. Method calls and receiver shorthand

**Today (verified):** [OD6](../docs/decisions.md#od6) fixes coherent dispatch and Trait::method qualification; [OD32](../docs/decisions.md#od32) fixes explicit receiver borrowing; [OD60](../docs/decisions.md#od60) and [TRAIT-9](../legacy/docs/spec/traits.md#TRAIT-9) fix one consuming receiver.

**Proposed change:** Remove dot calls; keep inherent associated calls and trait-qualified calls. Separately replace receiver shorthand with ordinary typed first parameters, preserving the consuming Destroy protocol. **Lost:** Chaining and receiver shorthand.

**Verdicts:** Codex **STRONG**; Kimi **STRONG**; agy **ASK**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** Two reviewers strongly favor explicit call targets; the third asks the same question. Qualified calls expose dispatch without removing traits or bounds. Receiver declaration migration needs its own explicit approval, especially Destroy.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-12 receiver alternatives and part of OPEN-3 disappear; field projection remains OPEN-20.

```con
// Before
 (&s).m(x);
 // After: same trait implementation
 Tr::m(&s, x);
```
## 2. Two map families and their compiler status

**Today (verified):** [approved slices](../ROADMAP.md#vertical-slices) includes both maps at 23; Q2.2 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) excludes HashMap from the initial Destroy inventory; Q2.3 specifies OrderedMap destruction order. Q9.2/Q9.6 distinguish ordinary owning definitions from irreducible primitives.

**Proposed change:** Defer HashMap pending a measured need and complete contracts; retain OrderedMap. Review whether map names need compiler privilege independently. **Lost:** Expected constant-time lookup and potentially useful performance.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **ASK**; agy **ASK**.

**Merged: ASK OWNER.** Two reviewers question map scope. Ordered lookup is not a proven substitute for hashing workloads. Neither the reserved-name proposal nor slice placement proves both maps must be compiler primitives; decide workload and semantic obligations before representation.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-4 builtin inventory and OPEN-21 signatures shrink if HashMap is deferred.
## 3. Value blocks and statement/value if/match

**Today (verified):** [OD77](../docs/decisions.md#od77) retains value forms and explicit function returns; [OD86](../docs/decisions.md#od86) narrows arm bodies; [approved slices](../ROADMAP.md#vertical-slices) explicitly adds branch tails at slice 3.

**Proposed change:** agy offers single-expression branches, explicit yield, or removal of value forms; retain value forms and complete their common-prefix grammar. **Lost:** If removed: immutable branch construction and direct production of one linear owner per path.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **STRONG**.

**Merged: KEEP.** Value branches express an ownership distinction useful to readers and checking. Parser difficulty alone does not justify outer mutable temporaries or a new yield construct. agy’s proposed uninitialized outer let is also not established syntax. Keep behavior while closing the grammar.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-16 remains; none of agy’s restrictions is silently adopted.
## 4. Point-local proofs versus function proof attributes

**Today (verified):** [OD79](../docs/decisions.md#od79) extended by [SPARK](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06) adds assert(e) by thm(...); [no hidden traps](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-no-hidden-traps) defines function-level #[proof(path)].

**Proposed change:** Keep both evidence scopes; agy asks whether one hint mechanism can replace them. **Lost:** Removing either loses a local proved fact or a way to discharge/functionally describe a function obligation.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **KEEP**; agy **ASK**.

**Merged: KEEP.** The scopes and claims differ: a local assertion introduces a fact at that point; a function attribute connects a theorem to function obligations or properties. Shared infrastructure is appropriate, but one spelling cannot be removed merely because both name theorems.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-13 theorem argument grammar and OPEN-15 attachment remain.
## 5. Constructor field punning

**Today (verified):** [OD25](../docs/decisions.md#od25)/[OD84](../docs/decisions.md#od84)/[OD130](../docs/decisions.md#od130) establish named patterns and explicit ignore handling; expression puns remain proposed in grammar OPEN-20, not a separately verified deciding row.

**Proposed change:** Require field: expression in construction; keep pattern policy separate. **Lost:** Only abbreviated constructors when field and local names coincide.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **STRONG**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** Explicit constructor values separate labels from consumed locals. This is a small surface reduction with little cost to checking or reading. Codex’s grammar review also favors it, but that is not a simplification-review verdict and is not counted as consensus here.

**Grammar interaction:** Closes the expression-pun choice in OPEN-20 if approved.

```con
// Before (v1 proposal)
let s: S = S { x };
// After
let s: S = S { x: x };
```
## 6. Pattern field punning

**Today (verified):** [OD84](../docs/decisions.md#od84) and [OD77](../docs/decisions.md#od77) retain destructuring/renaming; [OD25](../docs/decisions.md#od25) fixes explicit ignored fields; [PAT-10/11](../legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md#PAT-10) use bare field binders.

**Proposed change:** agy proposes field: binder everywhere; retain the existing same-name binder form. **Lost:** If removed: concise same-name destructuring and familiar binding syntax.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **STRONG**.

**Merged: KEEP.** In a pattern, a field name already introduces its same-name binder; it does not silently consume an existing local. Duplicating every binder offers less clarity than explicit constructor values. The decided rename and ignore forms remain visible alternatives for genuinely different bindings.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-17 retained; do not infer pattern-pun removal from constructor-pun removal.
## 7. Mathematical versus machine arithmetic notation

**Today (verified):** [OD12](../docs/decisions.md#od12) distinguishes contract mathematics from machine arithmetic; [OD145](../docs/decisions.md#od145) selects named ARITH-4 machine operations inside contracts.

**Proposed change:** Keep both domains, but require an explicit mathematical boundary spelling in contracts. **Lost:** Compact unmarked mathematical expressions.

**Verdicts:** Codex **STRONG**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** The same operator has different overflow meaning in runtime and contract positions. Marking the domain makes review safer without deleting mathematical reasoning. Exact boundary syntax and its scope need owner approval; this is a proposed revision, not the current rule.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-13 contract grammar gains an explicit domain boundary if approved.

```con
// Before
#[ensures(result == x + y)]
// After — ILLUSTRATIVE: math spelling undecided
#[ensures(math { result == x + y })]
```
## 8. Expression as casts

**Today (verified):** [OD11](../docs/decisions.md#od11) admits only lossless-domain as conversions; [OD91](../docs/decisions.md#od91) requires generic-target parentheses; [OD98](../docs/decisions.md#od98) gates reference-to-raw conversion; Q3.9 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) uses expose/from_exposed.

**Proposed change:** Replace expression as with named exact conversion operations; retain as for binding aliases. **Lost:** Infix cast notation.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **STRONG**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** Named exact conversion can remove a precedence level and the range-bound delimiter exception. agy overstates today’s casts: pointer/integer round trips are explicit provenance operations, not blanket as casts, and there is no verified trait-conversion as mechanism. Keep every conversion’s existing safety and provenance contract.

**Grammar interaction:** Removes cast-target portions of OPEN-8/14 and cast-delimiter portion of OPEN-19, not the remaining borrow/defer questions.

```con
// Before
let n: u64 = x as u64;
// After — ILLUSTRATIVE: widen name undecided
let n: u64 = widen::<u64>(x);
```
## 9. Heap move-out written *h

**Today (verified):** [OD59](../docs/decisions.md#od59) explicitly chooses *h plus destroy(h); [OD13](../docs/decisions.md#od13) separately requires read_owned for raw ownership transfer; [OD36](../docs/decisions.md#od36) fixes scoped heap opening.

**Proposed change:** Replace consuming heap-star with one named move-out operation; keep reference/raw dereference. **Lost:** One-character heap unboxing.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **STRONG**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** Heap move-out also releases storage, unlike an ordinary reference dereference. A named operation exposes that effect while retaining the distinction between move-out and destruction. The name must avoid reviving the removed generic unwrap/free/take APIs without an explicit decision.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-20 dereference classification becomes smaller; OPEN-21 needs the new signature.

```con
// Before
let value: T = *h;
// After — ILLUSTRATIVE: into_inner name undecided
let value: T = into_inner(h);
```
## 10. Parentheses on assertions and assumptions

**Today (verified):** [OD79](../docs/decisions.md#od79) adds assert; [OD80](../docs/decisions.md#od80) keeps tracked assume, qualified by [no hidden traps](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-no-hidden-traps); [SPARK](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06) fixes the parenthesized assert(e) by suffix.

**Proposed change:** Require assert(e); and assume(e); uniformly, retaining the theorem suffix only on assert. **Lost:** Unparenthesized forms.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **STRONG**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** One delimited condition grammar is easier to read and avoids the special grouped-root eligibility rule for by. This revises accepted forms; v2 therefore keeps the existing proposal until the owner chooses, rather than presenting new parentheses as already decided.

**Grammar interaction:** Closes the assertion-parenthesis part of OPEN-13, not spec bodies or proof scopes.

```con
// Before
assert x > 0;
assume ready;
// After
assert(x > 0);
assume(ready);
```
## 11. Link/export attribute payload punctuation

**Today (verified):** [OD96](../docs/decisions.md#od96) and [FFI-5](../legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#FFI-5) fix foreign symbol identity; exact = versus parentheses payload remains OPEN-15.

**Proposed change:** Use #[link_name("symbol")] and #[export_name("symbol")], like other parameterized attributes. **Lost:** The = payload spelling proposed in v1.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **STRONG**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** This removes an unnecessary attribute-argument convention. Symbol meaning and linkage stay the same. No existing decision is being claimed to approve the replacement punctuation.

**Grammar interaction:** Closes the link/export payload part of OPEN-15.

```con
// Before (v1 proposal)
#[link_name = "c_read"]
// After — ILLUSTRATIVE: payload punctuation unapproved
#[link_name("c_read")]
```
## 12. Different import and reference path separators

**Today (verified):** [SYN-10](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-10) documents dotted imports; [OD77](../docs/decisions.md#od77) approves import-related grammar resync; [OD151](../docs/decisions.md#od151) admits multilevel :: references.

**Proposed change:** Use :: for module paths in imports as well. **Lost:** Dotted import notation.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **STRONG**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** Modules have one path structure; sharing its separator across imports and references removes a needless reading convention. This is independent of whether imports bind bare names or aliases. Final list punctuation still requires approval.

**Grammar interaction:** Replaces the dot-boundary question in OPEN-11 with one :: list form.

```con
// Before
import a.b.{f};
// After — ILLUSTRATIVE: import separator unapproved
import a::b::{f};
```
## 13. char as a distinct byte type

**Today (verified):** [TYPE-20](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-20) defines a byte code unit and u8 round trips; [OD137](../docs/decisions.md#od137) restricts literal characters to ASCII; [OD42](../docs/decisions.md#od42) defines comparisons.

**Proposed change:** Remove char; retain ASCII quoted literals typed u8 and explicit UTF-8 text operations. **Lost:** A distinct type suggesting textual intent.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **STRONG**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** Today char carries no Unicode-scalar invariant and invites that misreading. A byte type plus ASCII literal notation is clearer for byte-oriented code. This changes literal and pattern typing and overloads, not UTF-8 validity of String or StaticStr.

**Grammar interaction:** Simplifies OPEN-4/6/17/21, but quoted-token lexical rules still need approval.

```con
// Before
let c: char = 'A';
// After — ILLUSTRATIVE: revised literal typing
let c: u8 = 'A';
```
## 14. Special output and append forms

**Today (verified):** [OD133](../docs/decisions.md#od133) reserves print/println/append; [OD154](../docs/decisions.md#od154) requires Alloc for allocating strings; Q7.10/11 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) require grants and Console for streams.

**Proposed change:** Remove special variadic/closed-overload forms; use ordinary byte output and typed string operations. **Lost:** Concise formatting, newline sugar and special append overloading.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **STRONG**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** Ordinary typed calls expose allocation, failure and authority using mechanisms already needed elsewhere. The replacement API must conserve linear errors and grants; no candidate signature is presumed already decided. An ordinary function may still provide a useful operation without compiler-special variadic syntax.

**Grammar interaction:** Shrinks OPEN-4/21 name and signature closure; does not remove Console or grants.

```con
// Before: special-form sketch
println("ok");
// After — ILLUSTRATIVE: byte-output API/signature undecided
match write_bytes(&mut out, "ok\n") { Result::Ok { value: _ } => {}, Result::Err { err } => { handle_io(err); }, }
```
## 15. Omitted binding and result types

**Today (verified):** [slice-0 decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-slice0-surface-2026-11-06) requires typed lets; [OD157](../docs/decisions.md#od157) names Unit; ordinary local/result omission is described in the inherited grammar, with closure OPEN-9/18.

**Proposed change:** Require explicit local types and every result arrow, including -> Unit. Preserve decided argument-based generic inference. **Lost:** Shorter declarations.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **STRONG**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: CHANGE.** Local type visibility helps reading and keeps declaration style uniform across slices. This is a proposal to extend the slice-0 discipline, not evidence that OD157 already bans omitted Unit results. Pattern binder annotations and ghost typing need a specific compatible rule.

**Grammar interaction:** Closes ordinary omission choices in OPEN-9/18 and part of OPEN-22 function types.

```con
// Before
fn f() { let n = make_n(); discard(n); return; }
// After
fn f() -> Unit { let n: u64 = make_n(); discard(n); return; }
```
## 16. Process as a currently unused capability

**Today (verified):** [authority rule 13](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority) reserves Process; [OD136](../docs/decisions.md#od136) removes process_exit; [OD156](../docs/decisions.md#od156) moves args to Env; Q7.4 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) defers spawning.

**Proposed change:** Remove Process only until a target supplies process operations and grants. **Lost:** A future-facing capability name and the ability for foreign declarations to name it today.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **STRONG**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: ASK OWNER.** A reserved but unused permission is questionable, but deleting it changes the closed authority universe and potentially foreign signatures. Confirm that no intended foreign boundary needs it before removal. This narrowly concerns an atom; it does not reopen capabilities plus grants.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-3/4/14 tables shrink if approved.
## 17. Late-read deferred arguments

**Today (verified):** Q9.8 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) explicitly chooses late reads and nested deferred scopes; [OD2](../docs/decisions.md#od2) holds deferred loans; [OD144](../docs/decisions.md#od144) places ensures after cleanup.

**Proposed change:** Consider evaluating/capturing arguments when defer is registered, retaining explicit ownership and loans. **Lost:** Mutating a resource after scheduling cleanup that will later read its final state.

**Verdicts:** Codex **ASK**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: ASK OWNER.** The call-like spelling invites eager-evaluation expectations, but late reads enable important cleanup patterns. Test concrete buffer/file examples before changing ownership timing. Keep defer; removing it would repeat cleanup across exits.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-19 syntax can remain; semantics and loan timing would change.
## 18. Ordinary bodyless functions

**Today (verified):** [OD77](../docs/decisions.md#od77) explicitly retains bodyless ; syntax; trait and extern declarations already have specific roles.

**Proposed change:** Refuse ordinary prototypes unless a demonstrated checked-interface format requires them; retain trait signatures and extern declarations. **Lost:** Standalone prototypes or a future separate-interface form.

**Verdicts:** Codex **ASK**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: ASK OWNER.** Definitions can be collected independently of source order, reducing declaration/definition matching. Generated interfaces at slice 17 may justify a precise use, however; verify that requirement before deleting an already-decided form.

**Grammar interaction:** Can close ordinary bodyless placement in OPEN-9.
## 19. General packed structures

**Today (verified):** [OD111](../docs/decisions.md#od111) permits misaligned fields but refuses borrowing them; [OD147](../docs/decisions.md#od147) permits combined C/packed layout.

**Proposed change:** Remove general packed records unless a real packed foreign ABI requires them; decode wire formats explicitly. **Lost:** Packed C ABI compatibility and compact records.

**Verdicts:** Codex **ASK**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: ASK OWNER.** Alignment exceptions add real proof and access obligations. File formats alone do not require packed language records or define endianness. A required packed C interface would justify keeping this feature; collect that evidence first.

**Grammar interaction:** Would remove packed alternatives and some validation from OPEN-15.
## 20. Local assume statements

**Today (verified):** [OD80](../docs/decisions.md#od80) keeps assumed claims tracked; [no hidden traps](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-no-hidden-traps) forbids assume from admitting safe operations.

**Proposed change:** Remove local assume; put necessary assumptions in named external/trusted contracts with propagated evidence identities. **Lost:** Local proof exploration and conditional non-safety claims.

**Verdicts:** Codex **ASK**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: ASK OWNER.** Named assumptions are easier to audit, but local assumptions may express legitimate conditional theorems. Moving them into wrappers can add boilerplate without removing any uncertainty. Require a concrete example and evidence-scope comparison.

**Grammar interaction:** Would remove assume grammar from OPEN-13; assumptions in evidence remain.
## 21. First-class existential brands

**Today (verified):** Q1.1–Q1.4/Q1.13 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) decide erased brands, existential loop state, explicit packing and fresh post-reset identity.

**Proposed change:** agy proposes lexical brands only, removing user existential packaging; preserve decided freshness and packaging pending a viable replacement. **Lost:** Heterogeneously branded storage and loop-carried fresh-brand state.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **ASK**.

**Merged: KEEP.** Fresh reset generations cannot safely be replaced by reusing a brand merely because no views are active. agy’s workaround conflicts with Q1.13 and does not establish equivalent expressiveness. Surface syntax can remain small while preserving existential meaning.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-22 still needs binder/escape grammar; removal would require revising Core Q1.
## 22. Function values and higher-order safety contracts

**Today (verified):** [OD93](../docs/decisions.md#od93) fixes exact function capability sets; Q2.4 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) uses a callback for drain; [SPARK](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06) and [approved slices](../ROADMAP.md#vertical-slices) require function-type safety contracts before slice 20. [OD116](../docs/decisions.md#od116) admits no ordinary total-function category; agy’s total-callback option would need to respect that or explicitly revise it.

**Proposed change:** agy proposes no function values or only precondition-free total callbacks; retain decided values while asking whether a restricted subset meets drain/map_into workloads. **Lost:** Indirect handlers, callbacks with preconditions or nontermination permissions.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **ASK**.

**Merged: ASK OWNER.** Indirect dispatch is explicit and useful. Restricting callbacks might reduce contract complexity, but must preserve resource-conserving drain and stated termination policy. No proof was supplied that showcase dispatch and cleanup fit the proposed subset; do not assert removal is free.

**Grammar interaction:** Could narrow OPEN-22 contracts and OPEN-15 expression permissions; neither disappears automatically.
## 23. Constants evaluated at each runtime use

**Today (verified):** [TYPE-22](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-22) gives per-use runtime evaluation; Q6.4 in [full Core rows](../docs/archive/decisions-2026-11-05/core_rows.json) expressly keeps it, while Q6.2 memoizes static known-value evaluation.

**Proposed change:** Consider closed total constant initializers and substitution of checked values; otherwise use named functions for repeated computation. **Lost:** Pure named computations outside the closed evaluator and per-use evaluation semantics.

**Verdicts:** Codex **not raised**; Kimi **ASK**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: ASK OWNER.** Distinguish the compile-time fact evaluator from runtime initializer evaluation; they are not contradictory decisions. Restricting const could make cost clearer, but broad compile-time execution remains refused. Define the admitted total subset and verify ownership before changing semantics.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-10 declaration spelling remains; semantic initializer closure becomes smaller.
## 24. Counted loops versus while

**Today (verified):** [OD47](../docs/decisions.md#od47) fixes both forms and one Core lowering; [OD49](../docs/decisions.md#od49) makes the counted measure mathematical, never runtime subtraction.

**Proposed change:** Retain counted loops; remove no loop form. **Lost:** If removed: once-evaluated bounds, immutable index and structural termination evidence.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **KEEP**.

**Merged: KEEP.** The counted form exposes a stronger iteration contract that handwritten while obscures. The Core already has one loop form, so shared lowering supplies implementation simplicity without losing reader-visible restrictions.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-18 labels remain; no new loop variant is suggested.
## 25. Plain, checked, wrapping and saturating arithmetic

**Today (verified):** [OD10](../docs/decisions.md#od10)/[OD145](../docs/decisions.md#od145), Q6.2 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) and [no hidden traps](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-no-hidden-traps) define distinct outcomes; [OD99](../docs/decisions.md#od99)/[OD106](../docs/decisions.md#od106)/[OD107](../docs/decisions.md#od107) distinguish lossy conversions.

**Proposed change:** Keep the outcome families and named conversion distinctions. **Lost:** If collapsed: safety evidence, explicit recoverable failure, modular intent or clamping intent.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **KEEP**; agy **KEEP**.

**Merged: These operations solve different situations rather than offer duplicate spellings. Parsers need recoverable failure and crypto needs modular arithmetic. Uniform implementation definitions and a closed inventory simplify checking without concealing intent..** OPEN-21 exact signatures remain; this KEEP does not oppose replacing the as spelling with a named exact conversion.

**Grammar interaction:** None.
## 26. Inline references versus scoped borrow/views

**Today (verified):** [OD1](../docs/decisions.md#od1)/[OD58](../docs/decisions.md#od58)/[OD36](../docs/decisions.md#od36), Q3/Q4.7/Q9.5 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) distinguish call-duration loans and scoped heap/array/text views.

**Proposed change:** Keep inline reference arguments and the single scoped borrow family. **Lost:** If collapsed: short call loans or named multi-statement/view access.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **KEEP**; agy **KEEP**.

**Merged: These scopes serve different use cases. References cannot simply become ordinary stored let values. The decided one scoped form already unifies heap opening and ranges; removing it would weaken visible lifetime and bounds handling..** OPEN-19 bound details and OPEN-21 view type names remain.

**Grammar interaction:** None.
## 27. defer versus explicit Destroy/resource cleanup

**Today (verified):** [OD2](../docs/decisions.md#od2)/[OD60](../docs/decisions.md#od60)/[OD69](../docs/decisions.md#od69)/[OD144](../docs/decisions.md#od144) and Q2.1 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) separate scheduling, destruction and resource cleanup.

**Proposed change:** Keep explicit cleanup plus defer; one consuming Destroy protocol. **Lost:** If merged or removed: structured cleanup across early exits or honest resource-specific failure handling.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **KEEP**.

**Merged: defer schedules an explicit call; Destroy specifies a consuming operation. They do not substitute for one another, and no implicit drop fills the gap. Preserve linear conservation and explicit close errors..** OPEN-19 target grammar remains; independent eager-versus-late capture question stays above.

**Grammar interaction:** None.
## 28. Storage release, destruction, draining and secret wiping

**Today (verified):** [OD28](../docs/decisions.md#od28)/[OD59](../docs/decisions.md#od59)/[OD60](../docs/decisions.md#od60), Q2 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core), and [information flow](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-infoflow-2026-11-06) fix distinct obligations.

**Proposed change:** Keep semantic distinctions; share infrastructure where proofs permit. **Lost:** If unified: owned payload recovery, fallible cleanup, non-Destroy element conservation or honest wiping guarantees.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: KEEP.** Different ownership outcomes and external effects require different contracts. A single cleanup verb cannot safely replace consuming move-out, resource close, draining and secret erasure. This KEEP concerns meanings, not the separate proposal to rename *h.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-21 API closure remains.
## 29. Static/dynamic text and nominal distinctions

**Today (verified):** [OD65](../docs/decisions.md#od65)/[OD127](../docs/decisions.md#od127), Q4/Q9.2 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) and [TYPE-12](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-12) distinguish nominal identity, transparent aliases, UTF-8 and allocation.

**Proposed change:** Keep static text versus allocating strings, bytes versus UTF-8, and wrapper types versus transparent aliases. **Lost:** If collapsed: visible allocation/encoding differences or nominal identity, including zero-sized tokens.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: KEEP.** These distinctions carry invariants or ownership facts instead of merely alternative notation. Uniform operations and documentation can simplify the surface without erasing identity or implying hidden allocation.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-10 aliases and OPEN-21 text API details remain.
## 30. Specification functions, ghost names and Lean theorems

**Today (verified):** [OD81](../docs/decisions.md#od81) admits erased ghost bindings; [OD115](../docs/decisions.md#od115) requires total spec-function bodies; [OD117](../docs/decisions.md#od117) and P18 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) place richer frame/entry properties in Lean.

**Proposed change:** Keep these distinct specification mechanisms rather than collapsing them into executable functions. **Lost:** If collapsed: erased intermediate facts, reusable total specification definitions or richer external proofs.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **not raised**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: KEEP.** A ghost binding names a local proof value, a spec function defines a reusable total computation for specifications, and a Lean theorem carries proof. They occupy different scopes and evidence roles; removing their distinction would obscure erasure or proof obligations.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-13 still closes ghost/name grammar and spec-body punctuation.
## 31. with(...) permissions plus resource grants — closed

**Today (verified):** [authority rules 1–2](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority) and Q7.11 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core); owner reaffirmed KEEP on 2026-11-08 in the instruction for this review.

**Proposed change:** Retain with(...) plus grants, including Console distinct from Device; do not reopen the capability comparison. **Lost:** Nothing under KEEP; collapse would lose operation-class summaries or resource-scope precision.

**Verdicts:** Codex **KEEP**; Kimi **KEEP**; agy **not raised**.

**Merged: KEEP.** This is already the owner’s answer, not a candidate for another vote. Permissions describe what operations a function may perform; grant values identify accessible resources. Brands and foreign receipts separately carry allocator identity and retained ownership.

**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-4 transcription and OPEN-14 capability syntax remain; no capability/grant redesign proposed.

