86:Recommend reserving `spec`, `by`, `kept` and `Self` under OPEN-3 (included in the proposed list above); `while` is the decided loop keyword (OD47). `Self` has special type meaning under [TRAIT-9](../legacy/docs/spec/traits.md#TRAIT-9), and is not an ordinary free type name. Recommended contextual words: `self`; attribute names `proof`, `may_not_terminate`, `requires`, `ensures`, `invariant`, `variant`, `test`, `repr`, `link_name`, `export_name`; repr arguments `C`, `packed`, `align`. `result` is a special bound name only inside ensures. These contextual statuses, where not expressly settled, are OPEN-3. `self`, `repr`, `packed`, `align` were expressly left unchanged by OD90, not newly reserved by it.
88:Canonical builtin type names are **reserved declaration names**, not necessarily keyword tokens: `i8 i16 i32 i64 u8 u16 u32 u64 bool char f32 f64 Unit`, plus the builtin nominal constructors admitted by their slices (`Secret`, `StaticStr`, `Option`, `Result`, `Allocator`, `Heap`, `HeapArray`, `Vec`, `String`, `OrderedMap`, `HashMap`, `AllocFailure`, `ArithmeticError`, `OutOfRange`, `Kept`, etc.). [OD43](../docs/decisions.md#od43), [OD102](../docs/decisions.md#od102), [OD157](../docs/decisions.md#od157) fix collisions/canonical spellings; [TYPE-19](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-19) lists scalar names. Builtin function names cannot be redeclared ([OD133](../docs/decisions.md#od133), [OD153](../docs/decisions.md#od153)). The exact complete builtin/grant/primitive name inventory is **OPEN-4**; `etc.` here is an identified inventory gap, not a wildcard accepted by the parser. Compiler-owned `__` names, `user_main` and the `__destr_` binding prefix have legacy restrictions ([MOD-3](../legacy/docs/spec/modules.md#MOD-3), [SYN-3](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-3)); carry their exact scope for approval in OPEN-4.
107:Minus is an operator, not part of INT/FLOAT. Literal expected typing and range checking include negation ([OD31](../docs/decisions.md#od31), [OD63](../docs/decisions.md#od63), [OD138](../docs/decisions.md#od138)); an unconstrained literal is refused, not defaulted. Float literals round directly to their expected width; no lexical suffix is implied by that rule.
128:`'` and `"` delimit lexical tokens, not standalone expression operators. `..` is only a pattern payload-rest marker (slice 10), not a range expression or update. `->` is only a result arrow (5; main already 0). `=>` is the match-arm arrow (10), fixed by [OD128](../docs/decisions.md#od128). No postfix `?`, `->`, `++`, `--`, compound assignments, range `..=`, or implication operator is introduced. Maximal munch, the precise token inventory and adjacent-operator handling are **OPEN-7**, with [SYN-7](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-7)'s special split of nested type `>>` retained for approval. A forbidden construct may be recognized to issue a targeted diagnostic without being a valid production.
