_review/SIMPLIFY_MERGED.md:316:**Merged: KEEP.** Fresh reset generations cannot safely be replaced by reusing a brand merely because no views are active. agy’s workaround conflicts with Q1.13 and does not establish equivalent expressiveness. Surface syntax can remain small while preserving existential meaning.
_review/SIMPLIFY_MERGED.md:318:**Grammar interaction:** OPEN-22 still needs binder/escape grammar; removal would require revising Core Q1.
_review/SIMPLIFY_MERGED.md:321:**Today (verified):** [OD93](../docs/decisions.md#od93) fixes exact function capability sets; Q2.4 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) uses a callback for drain; [SPARK](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06) and [approved slices](../ROADMAP.md#vertical-slices) require function-type safety contracts before slice 20. [OD116](../docs/decisions.md#od116) admits no ordinary total-function category; agy’s total-callback option would need to respect that or explicitly revise it.
_review/SIMPLIFY_MERGED.md:332:**Today (verified):** [TYPE-22](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-22) gives per-use runtime evaluation; Q6.4 in [full Core rows](../docs/archive/decisions-2026-11-05/core_rows.json) expressly keeps it, while Q6.2 memoizes static known-value evaluation.
