_review/SIMPLIFY_MERGED.md:420:**Today (verified):** [authority rules 1–2](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority) and Q7.11 in [Core rows](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core); owner reaffirmed KEEP on 2026-11-08 in the instruction for this review.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:5:This is the byte/token/surface-language inventory for the independent frontend judgment in Core **Q8.3**, not the ANF syntax of Core. [Q8.3 and Q9.1](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) distinguish those objects. In particular, Core `copy`, `move`, fresh numeric identities and condition regions are not new source spellings.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:15:EBNF: `=` defines; `|` separates alternatives; `[x]` is optional; `{x}` repeats; quoted text is a token; `ε` is empty. `IDENT`, `INT`, `FLOAT`, `CHAR`, `STRING`, `LABEL`, `EOF` are token classes. Quoted identifier-shaped attribute names are contextual token tests, **not** automatically reserved words. `List(X)` and `List1(X)` below are explicitly defined list expansions. No uppercase/lowercase path heuristic is permitted: [OD152](../docs/decisions.md#od152).
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:17:Each grammar group has a slice/provenance table. Auxiliary productions inherit that group's slice, or the stated later extension. Slice numbers mean first availability of the form, not permission to use all its eventual operands immediately. The source is the [approved cumulative slice table](../ROADMAP.md#vertical-slices), under the [vertical-slices decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-vertical-slices-2026-11-06). The roadmap's LP0 adds no syntax.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:51:The slice-0 subset admits only its restricted `main` body, not arbitrary calls or declarations just because a later production appears here. Unsupported forms need classified refusals: [slice-0 decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-slice0-surface-2026-11-06).
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:57:UTF-8 source and UTF-8 static text are supported by [Core Q4.1–Q4.4](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core); the explicit legacy source-encoding and escape rule is [SYN-5](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-5). ASCII char literals are decided by [OD137](../docs/decisions.md#od137). Exact source whitespace, identifier alphabet and source byte edge cases lack a dedicated decision: **OPEN-1**, **OPEN-2**. Recommended lexical core:
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:69:Slices: identifier/space/source decoding 0; line comments recommended at 0; labels 4. `//` comments have no nesting; `/*…*/` is absent in [SYN-6](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-6), but its precise status as a current owner spelling choice is **OPEN-1**. LF, CR or EOF ends a comment; CRLF therefore ends it at CR, with LF remaining whitespace (OPEN-1 recommendation). A BOM, shebang, non-ASCII whitespace, Unicode identifiers, embedded source NUL are not silently accepted by this recommendation; see OPEN-1/2.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:71:Names are case-sensitive (recommended, OPEN-2), and casing does not determine a path's syntactic category ([OD152](../docs/decisions.md#od152)). `_` is an unused binding, not a license to lose a linear value or Option/Result: [OD62](../docs/decisions.md#od62), [audit](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-audit).
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:84:Explicit decisions: `from`/`until` [OD50](../docs/decisions.md#od50); `ghost` [OD81](../docs/decisions.md#od81); `Copy` [OD90](../docs/decisions.md#od90); the nine capabilities, including `Console`, [authority rule 13](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority), as revised by [Q7.11](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core). [OD73](../docs/decisions.md#od73) forbids reserved words in identifier positions, including import aliases and variant names. The entropy capability arrives at slice 6, but its **name is not supplied by that decision**: [stack/randomness decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-stack-randomness). Do not reintroduce the historical capability `Random` without approval.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:88:Canonical builtin type names are **reserved declaration names**, not necessarily keyword tokens: `i8 i16 i32 i64 u8 u16 u32 u64 bool char f32 f64 Unit`, plus the builtin nominal constructors admitted by their slices (`Secret`, `StaticStr`, `Option`, `Result`, `Allocator`, `Heap`, `HeapArray`, `Vec`, `String`, `OrderedMap`, `HashMap`, `AllocFailure`, `ArithmeticError`, `OutOfRange`, `Kept`, etc.). [OD43](../docs/decisions.md#od43), [OD102](../docs/decisions.md#od102), [OD157](../docs/decisions.md#od157) fix collisions/canonical spellings; [TYPE-19](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-19) lists scalar names. Builtin function names cannot be redeclared ([OD133](../docs/decisions.md#od133), [OD153](../docs/decisions.md#od153)). The exact complete builtin/grant/primitive name inventory is **OPEN-4**; `etc.` here is an identified inventory gap, not a wildcard accepted by the parser. Compiler-owned `__` names, `user_main` and the `__destr_` binding prefix have legacy restrictions ([MOD-3](../legacy/docs/spec/modules.md#MOD-3), [SYN-3](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-3)); carry their exact scope for approval in OPEN-4.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:105:Decimal integers arrive at 0; other bases at 2; FLOAT at 26; STRING/CHAR at 16 (a reason STRING in an earlier annotation is metadata, not a runtime StaticStr feature). Leading-zero decimal integers are explicitly refused: [slice-0 surface](../docs/decisions.md#decided-slice0-surface-2026-11-06). The old forms are documented by [SYN-6](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-6). **OPEN-5**: approve lowercase base prefixes, no separators, float digit/point syntax and a minimal typed-integer suffix policy and boundary handling; the frozen lexer also accepted uppercase prefixes. The [approved Q6.2 field example](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-q6-2-fields) contains `200u8`. A blanket suffix refusal conflicts with that example; OPEN-5 recommends retaining typed integer suffixes, but their complete width/base/boundary grammar needs approval. The displayed INT production is the unsuffixed kernel, not a complete suffix grammar. No exponent notation, `1.`, `.5`, hex floats or special NaN/Inf literals are proposed.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:116:No `\xHH`, `\u{…}`, interpolation, raw-string delimiter or byte-string prefix is admitted by this proposal. Embedded NUL in static text is explicitly permitted by Core Q4.2, using `\0`; ASCII literal restrictions do not restrict every computed `char` to 0…127 ([TYPE-20](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-20)). A char ending in a closing quote takes priority over LABEL; a bare apostrophe plus a name is LABEL. The exact lexical distinction and malformed-quote refusal is OPEN-6, not a token-level LL(1) claim about individual bytes.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:128:`'` and `"` delimit lexical tokens, not standalone expression operators. `..` is only a pattern payload-rest marker (slice 10), not a range expression or update. `->` is only a result arrow (5; main already 0). `=>` is the match-arm arrow (10), fixed by [OD128](../docs/decisions.md#od128). No postfix `?`, `->`, `++`, `--`, compound assignments, range `..=`, or implication operator is introduced. Maximal munch, the precise token inventory and adjacent-operator handling are **OPEN-7**, with [SYN-7](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-7)'s special split of nested type `>>` retained for approval. A forbidden construct may be recognized to issue a targeted diagnostic without being a valid production.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:132:Precedence, low to high, from [SYN-2](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-2) and the [frozen grammar](../legacy/grammar/concrete.ebnf); the complete table lacks a dedicated decided row, so **OPEN-8** requests ratification:
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:150:`-x as i32` means `(-x) as i32`; `-c.n` means `-(c.n)`. Assignment is a statement, not a precedence level. Left grouping of comparisons does not make a type-invalid chain legal. [OD91](../docs/decisions.md#od91) explicitly decides `x as T < y` as comparison and `x as (Vec<T>)` for a generic cast target.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:208:| program, main function shell, function_block | 0 | [slice-0 decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-slice0-surface-2026-11-06); arbitrary functions/signatures at 5 |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:209:| item prefixes, `pub`, `trusted fn`, `trusted extern fn` | 17 / 24 / 25 | [OD9](../docs/decisions.md#od9), [OD22](../docs/decisions.md#od22), [OD61](../docs/decisions.md#od61); prefix order/allowed targets **OPEN-9** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:212:| enum/variants | 10 | [OD71](../docs/decisions.md#od71), [OD72](../docs/decisions.md#od72), [OD77](../docs/decisions.md#od77); exact declaration punctuation **OPEN-9** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:213:| type alias | 9 | feature in slice table; [TYPE-12](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-12) evidence; `type N = T;` **OPEN-10** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:214:| const | 17 | [OD8](../docs/decisions.md#od8), [Q6.4](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core); `const N: T = e;` **OPEN-10** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:215:| mod | 17 | `mod X;` [OD78](../docs/decisions.md#od78), no inline body [OD33](../docs/decisions.md#od33); file X.con, children in X/ [OD142](../docs/decisions.md#od142) |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:217:| trait/impl/method heads | 14; generic impl 14 using slice-11 parameters | qualified calls [OD6](../docs/decisions.md#od6); trait parameters forbidden [OD148](../docs/decisions.md#od148); generic trait methods forbidden [OD77](../docs/decisions.md#od77); precise heads/receiver punctuation **OPEN-12** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:219:| extern_rest/extern_param | 25 | `extern fn` [OD4](../docs/decisions.md#od4); explicit with [FFI-3](../legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md#FFI-3); marker `kept` and receipt `Kept<H>` [Q3.12](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core); `kept buf: H` and unmarked call-only default already decided; remaining API qualification **OPEN-23** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:221:Empty structs are legal, empty enums are refused. Commas between fields/variants are mandatory; trailing-comma availability in each list is OPEN-9/11/14, not permission to omit separators. Trait declarations have neither type nor capability parameters; trait methods have no generic list; trait impls cannot declare capability parameters ([OD89](../docs/decisions.md#od89)). `impl Trait for Type` is recommended, matching the actual parser; the stale EBNF comment reverses it. Coherence, orphan checks and the Copy/Destroy-disjoint impl exception are name/type judgments ([OD6](../docs/decisions.md#od6), [Core Q2.8](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core)). They do not require disjunctive-bound syntax.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:246:| `#[requires(e)]`, `#[ensures(e)]` | 5 | [OD125](../docs/decisions.md#od125) discusses these forms; [CON-2](../legacy/docs/spec/contracts.md#CON-2); function declarations; logical claims, safety use requires evidence |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:247:| `#[invariant(e)]`, `#[variant(e)]` | 4 | [OD82](../docs/decisions.md#od82), [OD104](../docs/decisions.md#od104), [OD105](../docs/decisions.md#od105); next loop; a counted-loop variant is refused |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:251:| `#[test]` | 8 | [OD146](../docs/decisions.md#od146), revised [main decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-main): result u8 only; parameterless per [STMT-10](../legacy/docs/spec/statements.md#STMT-10), not reopened by OPEN-15 |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:252:| struct `#[invariant(e)]` | 17 | [SPARK decision/revision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06); struct with private fields; exact field names/self scope **OPEN-15** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:256:A declaration attribute attaches to the next declaration; loop attributes to the next loop, not a freestanding item ([OD82](../docs/decisions.md#od82)). Repeated requires/invariants mean conjunction ([CON-8](../legacy/docs/spec/contracts.md#CON-8)); duplicate options and other repeatability details are OPEN-15. Packed plus align is refused; alignment is a power of two within FFI-4's constraint; C plus packed means C order, no padding, alignment 1 ([OD147](../docs/decisions.md#od147)). Enums have no repr form. Default layout was revised to declaration order/natural alignment in the [runtime decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-runtime-2026-11-06); the old “unspecified layout” prose does not override it.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:295:| arguments, cap_name | 11 | expression capability arguments [OD87](../docs/decisions.md#od87), shape/order [OD88](../docs/decisions.md#od88), symbolic unions [Q5.2](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core); bare reserved capability atom and delimiters **OPEN-14** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:296:| cap_clause | 6; variables 11 | [authority](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority), [OD108](../docs/decisions.md#od108); names/variables only, no repeated names, no user aliases; exact union use inside with **OPEN-14** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:297:| named_type | scalars 0/2/3/16/26, structs 1/9, enums 10, applications 11, qualified 17 | [OD43](../docs/decisions.md#od43), [OD151](../docs/decisions.md#od151), [OD152](../docs/decisions.md#od152); punctuation **OPEN-14** where not fixed |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:298:| reference type | 13 | [OD1](../docs/decisions.md#od1), [OD2](../docs/decisions.md#od2), [OD14](../docs/decisions.md#od14): second-class, no stored/returned refs |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:300:| function type | 20 | exact capability sets [OD93](../docs/decisions.md#od93); `fn(&mut C, T) with(K) -> Step<T, E>` [Q2.4](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core); function-type safety contracts **OPEN-22** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:304:Semantic filters: ordinary generic type arguments precede capability arguments (OD88); explicit capability arguments are mandatory at every polymorphic call ([Q5.1/Q5.4 revision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-revisions)); type arguments may be inferred from checked argument types only ([OD46](../docs/decisions.md#od46)), and enum literals follow that same argument-based rule, with explicit arguments otherwise, never inference from an expected result type ([OD129](../docs/decisions.md#od129)). A singleton name is classified by its declaration and parameter kind, never initial case. Unions contain names only, not composite types. `{}` denotes the empty capability set; it is not an empty type argument list. Exact set equality, no widening, no `with(f)` callback shortcut ([OD92](../docs/decisions.md#od92), [OD93](../docs/decisions.md#od93)).
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:335:Slices: let name/binder 0; empty struct destructuring 1; named field patterns 9; match/variant/OR/rest 10; CHAR patterns no earlier than char at 16. `binder` may be `_`; it is not a general binding catch-all pattern in match. Recommended bare match IDENT is only `_`; bare qualified path denotes a fieldless enum variant. Irrefutable enum lets and mutable pattern binders are retained ([PAT-10/11](../legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md#PAT-10)); the factored let path admits module-qualified struct and enum heads, subject to OPEN-17 exact path closure. Nested patterns remain deferred, and fields must be handled explicitly or through the decided ignore forms (OD25). Generic pattern paths such as `E::<T>::V` are accepted by the frozen parser but not established by that fact as a new decision: OPEN-17 must explicitly disposition them; the kernel above does not yet include their arguments. Char literal patterns and the precise payload-rest combination grammar remain OPEN-17.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:339:Decisions: struct destructuring [OD84](../docs/decisions.md#od84); binding renaming [OD77](../docs/decisions.md#od77); named fields and `_` [OD25](../docs/decisions.md#od25), [OD130](../docs/decisions.md#od130); no unqualified struct match pattern [OD76](../docs/decisions.md#od76); no guards [OD55](../docs/decisions.md#od55); no ranges [OD56](../docs/decisions.md#od56); unbraced arm restricted to expression/block/return [OD86](../docs/decisions.md#od86). The exact OR/arm-comma and pattern grammar inherited from [PAT-1/3](../legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md#PAT-1) is OPEN-17. `arm_expr` is the non-block-root expression alternative; `arm_block` is a block parsed once and checked for value/statement use (OPEN-16), preventing two `{` alternatives.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:386:| typed let/name/read/return | 0 | [slice-0 decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-slice0-surface-2026-11-06); unannotated let details **OPEN-18** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:391:| labels, break, continue | 4 | label support in slice table, `break <expr>` forbidden [OD27](../docs/decisions.md#od27); apostrophe/colon/target syntax **OPEN-18** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:392:| defer | 14 | [OD2](../docs/decisions.md#od2), canonical Unit-only [audit](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-audit); exact call grammar **OPEN-19** |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:393:| borrow_statement | 13/15/16/19/21 | section 6; [OD58](../docs/decisions.md#od58), [Core Q4.7](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) |
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:394:| assert and theorem suffix | 8 | [OD79](../docs/decisions.md#od79), [SPARK](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06); suffix only on parenthesized assertion per decided example; exact factoring **OPEN-13** |
