_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:615:Postfix `?` is a **decided permanent refusal**, through [P16/refusal statuses](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-refusals) and [the binding refusal list](../docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#what-concrete-refuses). OPEN-25 does not reopen it. Value `while … else` and postfix member `->` are documented removals in the [frozen grammar](../legacy/grammar/concrete.ebnf); no separate deciding row was located for those two. OPEN-25 requests ratification only for them. The function result arrow remains. Block-comment and exponent policy still needs OPEN-1/5 approval.
