5:This is the byte/token/surface-language inventory for the independent frontend judgment in Core **Q8.3**, not the ANF syntax of Core. [Q8.3 and Q9.1](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core) distinguish those objects. In particular, Core `copy`, `move`, fresh numeric identities and condition regions are not new source spellings.
57:UTF-8 source and UTF-8 static text are supported by [Core Q4.1–Q4.4](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core); the explicit legacy source-encoding and escape rule is [SYN-5](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-5). ASCII char literals are decided by [OD137](../docs/decisions.md#od137). Exact source whitespace, identifier alphabet and source byte edge cases lack a dedicated decision: **OPEN-1**, **OPEN-2**. Recommended lexical core:
84:Explicit decisions: `from`/`until` [OD50](../docs/decisions.md#od50); `ghost` [OD81](../docs/decisions.md#od81); `Copy` [OD90](../docs/decisions.md#od90); the nine capabilities, including `Console`, [authority rule 13](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority), as revised by [Q7.11](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core). [OD73](../docs/decisions.md#od73) forbids reserved words in identifier positions, including import aliases and variant names. The entropy capability arrives at slice 6, but its **name is not supplied by that decision**: [stack/randomness decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-stack-randomness). Do not reintroduce the historical capability `Random` without approval.
88:Canonical builtin type names are **reserved declaration names**, not necessarily keyword tokens: `i8 i16 i32 i64 u8 u16 u32 u64 bool char f32 f64 Unit`, plus the builtin nominal constructors admitted by their slices (`Secret`, `StaticStr`, `Option`, `Result`, `Allocator`, `Heap`, `HeapArray`, `Vec`, `String`, `OrderedMap`, `HashMap`, `AllocFailure`, `ArithmeticError`, `OutOfRange`, `Kept`, etc.). [OD43](../docs/decisions.md#od43), [OD102](../docs/decisions.md#od102), [OD157](../docs/decisions.md#od157) fix collisions/canonical spellings; [TYPE-19](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-19) lists scalar names. Builtin function names cannot be redeclared ([OD133](../docs/decisions.md#od133), [OD153](../docs/decisions.md#od153)). The exact complete builtin/grant/primitive name inventory is **OPEN-4**; `etc.` here is an identified inventory gap, not a wildcard accepted by the parser. Compiler-owned `__` names, `user_main` and the `__destr_` binding prefix have legacy restrictions ([MOD-3](../legacy/docs/spec/modules.md#MOD-3), [SYN-3](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-3)); carry their exact scope for approval in OPEN-4.
105:Decimal integers arrive at 0; other bases at 2; FLOAT at 26; STRING/CHAR at 16 (a reason STRING in an earlier annotation is metadata, not a runtime StaticStr feature). Leading-zero decimal integers are explicitly refused: [slice-0 surface](../docs/decisions.md#decided-slice0-surface-2026-11-06). The old forms are documented by [SYN-6](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-6). **OPEN-5**: approve lowercase base prefixes, no separators, float digit/point syntax and a minimal typed-integer suffix policy and boundary handling; the frozen lexer also accepted uppercase prefixes. The [approved Q6.2 field example](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-q6-2-fields) contains `200u8`. A blanket suffix refusal conflicts with that example; OPEN-5 recommends retaining typed integer suffixes, but their complete width/base/boundary grammar needs approval. The displayed INT production is the unsuffixed kernel, not a complete suffix grammar. No exponent notation, `1.`, `.5`, hex floats or special NaN/Inf literals are proposed.
116:No `\xHH`, `\u{…}`, interpolation, raw-string delimiter or byte-string prefix is admitted by this proposal. Embedded NUL in static text is explicitly permitted by Core Q4.2, using `\0`; ASCII literal restrictions do not restrict every computed `char` to 0…127 ([TYPE-20](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#TYPE-20)). A char ending in a closing quote takes priority over LABEL; a bare apostrophe plus a name is LABEL. The exact lexical distinction and malformed-quote refusal is OPEN-6, not a token-level LL(1) claim about individual bytes.
150:`-x as i32` means `(-x) as i32`; `-c.n` means `-(c.n)`. Assignment is a statement, not a precedence level. Left grouping of comparisons does not make a type-invalid chain legal. [OD91](../docs/decisions.md#od91) explicitly decides `x as T < y` as comparison and `x as (Vec<T>)` for a generic cast target.
